name: sim.loadModel
description: Loads a previously saved model, and selects it
luaSynopsis: a) int objectHandle = sim.loadModel(string filename) b) int objectHandle = sim.loadModel(bytes buffer) c) bytes rgbaImage = sim.loadModel(string filename, bool onlyThumbnail) d) bytes rgbaImage = sim.loadModel(bytes buffer, bool onlyThumbnail)
pythonSynopsis: a) int objectHandle = sim.loadModel(string filename) b) int objectHandle = sim.loadModel(buffer buffer) c) buffer rgbaImage = sim.loadModel(string filename, bool onlyThumbnail) d) buffer rgbaImage = sim.loadModel(buffer buffer, bool onlyThumbnail)
inputs:
1. filename: model filename. The filename extension is required (ttm, or simmodel.xml).
2. buffer: a buffer containing the model
3. onlyThumbnail: when true, then only the thumbnail image of the model is loaded and returned
outputs:
1. objectHandle: the handle of the model base object
2. rgbaImage: the model thumbnail image (128 x 128 x 4, rgba)
replacedBy:
- name: loadModel, class: scene, file: scene_loadModel.method
- name: loadModelFromBuffer, class: scene, file: scene_loadModelFromBuffer.method
- name: loadModelInfo, class: scene, file: scene_loadModelInfo.method
- name: loadModelInfoFromBuffer, class: scene, file: scene_loadModelInfoFromBuffer.method
